# Scaffold is a blank slate — never an auth screen first

When scaffolding or starting a new client project **before feature build / screen tickets**:

## Do

- Treat the repo as a **blank slate** with the stack, docs, and thin backend wiring the PRD named.
- First screen (web and mobile): product name + one short line of what it is (from the PRD). No sign-in, sign-up, or auth gate.
- Auth may exist as **infrastructure only** (Convex Auth tables, providers, env placeholders). That is not a reason to ship an auth UI.

## Do not

- Open the app on `/sign-in`, a password form, or any auth redirect before features are under build.
- Copy another job’s auth shell (including Ridgeway) as the starting UI.
- Assume “thin auth start” means “ship a sign-in screen.”

## When auth UI is allowed

Only after screen design and Linear tickets call for sign-in / sign-up as a product surface.

## Where this is also written

- `project-template/docs/new-project-scaffold.md` (authoritative for the copy list)

This is studio and client-repo behaviour. At scaffold, copy this file into the new client’s `.cursor/rules/` so agents in that window keep it.
